-    *   If $T \notin [min, max]$, prune the subtree (skip the node) [G].
-    *   If $T \in [min, max]$, descend into the children [S1][S3, unofficial].
-    *   *GPU Implementation Detail:* To compute entry and exit points efficiently, cubes corresponding to one level of the min/max octree can be rendered [S6]. All vertices of a cube have the same 2D texture coordinates containing the min/max values [S6]. Exit positions are computed by rendering cubes with `glCullFace(GL FRONT)` and `glDepthFunc(GL LESS)` [S6]. Entry positions are computed by rendering cubes again with `glCullFace(GL BACK)` and `glDepthFunc(GL GREATER)` [S6]. A fragment shader discards fragments if the cube is empty or does not contain the isosurface level [S6].
